  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 7313 Section 4 ('After the speaker completes the re-advertisement of the entire Adj-RIB-Out to the peer, it MUST send an EoRR message.'). In TestRFC7313EoRRFollowsTheRoutesItCloses (internal/component/bgp/reactor/rfc7313_refresh_order_test.go), only the test helper call changed from newSendPermissionReactor(peer) to newSendPermissionReactor(t, peer) so the test reactor publishes its compiled DeliveryGraph; all setup, inputs, and exact wire-order assertions are unchanged. Outside initial sync it proves exact wire sequence [eor, borr, route, eorr] with RefreshSent==2; during initial sync it proves no EoRR leaves while opQueue holds the route (RefreshSent==0) and drain preserves [borr, route, eorr, eor]. Alongside TestRouteRefreshSubtypes, TestRFC7313BoRRRoutesEoRRInOneSequence (JSON handleRefresh and DirectBridge handleRefreshStructured emitting BoRR, all IPv4 Adj-RIB-Out routes, then EoRR), TestRFC7313RefreshBracketsReadvertisementWithBoRRAndEoRR, and TestDispatchBGPPeerEoRR, both polarities enforce the requirement.",
